<h1>Thanos Sort</h1>
<p>
    Thanos Sort begins by checking if the array is sorted.
    If it is not sorted it removes half of the array elements at random.
    It repeats this process until the array is sorted.
    This usually results in only a couple of elements being left over from the original array.
    <br>
    <br>
    The Time Complexity of Thanos Sort depends on which method is being used to delete elements,
    with <b>Shifting</b> giving it a Time Complexity of <b>n<sup>2</sup></b>,
    and <b>Swapping</b> and <b>Gaps</b> giving it a Time Complexity of <b>n</b>.
</p>

